2026-10-12T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2312) 'A release tag is computed from its commit, so it sorts by time and parses everywhere.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2312) 'The orgs' releases carry four naming schemes and no rule. No single scheme among them sorts by time in a file listing and also parses as a version in Mix, Cargo, npm and Go.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2312) 'Run `elixir scripts/check_release_tags.exs` to recompute every tag, and read below for the later parts.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2312) 'release tags are go pseudo-versions
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2312) 'A release tag is `v0.0.0-<time>-<hash>`: the tagged commit's committer time in UTC as `YYYYMMDDhhmmss`, then the first 12 hex digits of the commit. It is the shape of a Go pseudo-version, and it is computed from the commit, never typed. The core stays `v0.0.0`. A stage, a rung name or a "1.0" goes in the release title and the stage branch, not in the tag. The operator chose the form on 2026-10-12 ("I like go's").
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2312) '- RFD66606-2294, interchangeable sessions: the stage branches this RFD leaves the stage to.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2312) '- RFD66606-2295, calibrated replies: the times here are UTC, as there.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2312) 'The three parts
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2312) 'The tag is the first of three parts of one release system. Each part does one job: identity is a hash, order is a fixed-width UTC time, stage is a pointer that moves, and compatibility is a version on the interface that breaks. The details give the later parts.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2312) 'Sources
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2312) 'Drafted on 2026-10-12 from the release inventory, the sort runs and the parser runs below, all taken the same day. The form and the "everywhere" bar are the operator's.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2312) 'What a tag has to satisfy
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2312) 'The operator's bar: a tag sorts in filesystem order, and the same string works everywhere a version is read. Measured on 2026-10-12, each candidate through each tool's own parser:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2312) '| Candidate | `ls` order | Mix | Cargo | npm | Go |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2312) '| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2312) '| `v2026.01.05`, padded calendar date | yes | no | no | no | no |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2312) '| `v2026.1.5`, unpadded calendar date | no | yes | yes | yes | yes |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2312) '| `v1.0.0-beta.1` and `v1.0.0` | no | yes | yes | yes | yes |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2312) '| `v0.0.0-20261012203512-50cc405a1b2c` | yes | yes | yes | yes | yes |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2312) '- SemVer forbids a leading zero in a number, so a padded month fails every package tool. Unpadded, `2026.10.12` sorts before `2026.9.1`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2312) '- No file listing puts a release after its own pre-releases: `ls`, `sort -V` and Finder all list `v1.0.0` before `v1.0.0-beta.1`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2312) '- The Go form carries the date inside one alphanumeric pre-release field, where SemVer allows the zeros. `ls`, `sort -V` and Finder each put samples from January, October, the next day and the next year in time order.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2312) '- Python's PEP 440 rejects the Go form. A Python package from the same commit is `0.0.0.devYYYYMMDDhhmmss`. Docker's tag grammar admits the form; no Docker daemon ran in the measurement.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2312) 'What others do
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2312) 'Read off the live registries on 2026-10-12. Builds between releases put an ISO basic date inside the pre-release: TypeScript `7.1.0-dev.20261012.1`, React `19.3.0-canary-9f2e1f88-20261012`, Node.js `v27.0.0-nightly202610123b639be3a4`, Go `v0.0.0-20261011100332-faecfb24eb49`. Calendar versions that must stay SemVer drop the padding: pip `26.2.1`, Home Assistant `2026.10.1`. Projects that list versions as strings pad instead: the Arch Linux ISOs, `YYYY.0M.0D` since 2012. Only Go's form, whose core never moves, sorts as plain bytes and parses as SemVer at once.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2312) 'The check
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2312) '`scripts/check_release_tags.exs` recomputes every tag from its commit:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2312) '    elixir scripts/check_release_tags.exs [<repo>]
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2312) '    elixir scripts/check_release_tags.exs --self-test
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2312) 'A tag on a commit from before 2026-10-13 is legacy, counted and named rather than failed; renaming a published tag breaks whatever points at it. The self-test plants six tags in a scratch repository. The commit's own pseudo-version passes; a seven-digit hash, a local-time stamp, a `v1.0.0` core, a padded calendar date and a stage-suffixed date each fail by name; a pre-cutover tag reads as legacy. Go's own `module.IsPseudoVersion` accepts a seven-digit hash, so the 12-digit rule is this check's, not Go's. Go does hold a pseudo-version to its commit's time and hash, which is why the tag is computed:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2312) '    TZ=UTC git log -1 --format='v0.0.0-%cd-%h' \
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2312) '      --date=format-local:%Y%m%d%H%M%S --abbrev=12
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2312) 'The later parts
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2312) 'Each part starts once the one before it runs.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2312) '1. The tag, this RFD.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2312) '2. The stage is a pointer. A moving tag per stage (`dev`, `beta`, `rc`, `release`) names the build that stage holds. Promotion moves the pointer to the same commit; nothing is rebuilt or renamed. The GitHub pre-release flag follows the pointer.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2312) '3. One release record per repository, and every other format derived from it. The Godot engine already works this way: `version.py` holds major, minor, patch and status; the build adds the commit hash and committer timestamp from git; the Windows resource takes `FILEVERSION` from the numbers; the Android build turns the status into a digit of `versionCode` (dev 1, alpha 2, beta 3). Here the record is the repository's `CITATION.cff` (operator, 2026-10-12), in two halves. The committed file holds what does not change per build: title, authors, licence, the interface versions. A commit cannot carry its own hash, so the release step writes the per-build half into the copy that ships with the artifact: `version` is the tag, `commit` the full hash, `date-released` the UTC date. CFF 1.2.0 admits no other top-level key; a `status` key fails its schema. The stage, the derived forms and the artifact digests ride as `identifiers` of type `other`: `stage:dev`, `windows:YYYY.MMDD.hhmm.0`, `android:<versionCode>`, `pep440:0.0.0.devYYYYMMDDhhmmss`, `sha256:<digest>`. A sample of that shape validates against the CFF 1.2.0 JSON schema. The check recomputes every derived value from the `commit` field.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2312) '4. Compatibility rides on the interface that breaks: a protocol, ABI or save-format version that moves only when that interface does, as Go moves a module path to `/v2`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2312) '5. A signed attestation binds the record to the artifact's digest.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2312) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2312) 'Of 60 GitHub releases in repositories pushed since 2026-06-01, 33 are SemVer pre-releases in at least four spellings, 7 are dates, 2 are plain SemVer and 18 are free names.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2312  1 LINE
 Text:Written
